<item><title>Quiet Forest</title><link>https://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/hiroshi-yoshimura-quiet-forest/</link><guid isPermaLink="false">https://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/hiroshi-yoshimura-quiet-forest</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:00:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Music Reviews</category><dc:creator>Pitchfork — Album reviews</dc:creator><description>Inspired by a visit to the Pacific Northwest, this 1996 record was the final album-length work released during the composer’s lifetime; it offers a rare glimpse of his most playful side.</description></item><item><title>Snakes &amp; Ladders</title><link>https://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/armand-hammer-snakes-and-ladders/</link><guid isPermaLink="false">https://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/armand-hammer-snakes-and-ladders</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:03:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Music Reviews</category><dc:creator>Pitchfork — Album reviews</dc:creator><description>It’s a marathon and the New York duo keeps the faith, delivering another lyrical masterclass over engrossing beats from the indie rap all-stars whose work they’ve cultivated.</description></item><item><title>Unfindable Ring</title><link>https://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/grumpy-unfindable-ring/</link><guid isPermaLink="false">https://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/grumpy-unfindable-ring</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:00:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Music Reviews</category><dc:creator>Pitchfork — Album reviews</dc:creator><description>The Brooklyn group prizes playfulness over conformity on its latest album, plumbing country, folk, indie rock, art pop, and more for an album of giddy love songs and existential gender trouble.</description></item><item><title>Cherry Soda</title><link>https://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/wavves-cherry-soda/</link><guid isPermaLink="false">https://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/wavves-cherry-soda</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:01:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Music Reviews</category><dc:creator>Pitchfork — Album